@startuml fix-findings-after
!include ../../theme.iuml
title fix-findings — with teamscale-mcp (ts_agent_helper replaced)

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

actor "Developer" as Dev
box "Developer workstation" $ws_bg
    participant "Claude\n(fix-findings skill)" as Agent
end box

box "Teamscale server" $ts_bg
    participant "teamscale-mcp\n(central sidecar)" as MCP
    participant "Teamscale\nREST API" as TS
end box

Dev -> Agent : /teamscale:fix-findings <file>
note over Agent : Identity = X-Teamscale-User / -Token,\nconfigured once in the MCP client.

note over Agent, MCP
  <b>Dropped:</b> the ts_agent_helper <b>.teamscale.toml</b> read.
  The agent now supplies <b>project + branch</b> as tool
  arguments itself — the sidecar reads no local config.
end note
Agent -[$tool_color,bold]> MCP : <size:15>**tool getFindings(project, uniformPath=<file>, branch)**</size>\nX-Teamscale-User + X-Teamscale-Token
activate MCP
MCP -> TS : GET /api/v2026.2/projects/{p}/findings/list\nAuthorization: Basic base64(user:token)
activate TS
TS --> MCP : findings JSON
deactivate TS
MCP --> Agent : findings (tool result)
deactivate MCP

opt finding type unclear
    Agent -[$tool_color,bold]> MCP : <size:15>**tool getFindingTypeDescriptions(typeIds, scope)**</size>
    MCP -> TS : POST /api/v2026.2/projects/{p}/finding-type-descriptors
    TS --> MCP : type descriptions
    MCP --> Agent : type descriptions
end

Agent -> Agent : triage by severity,\nread code, edit files to fix

opt false positive / toleration (after explicit user OK)
    Agent -[$tool_color,bold]> MCP : <size:15>**tool flagFindings(ids, type, rationale)**</size>
    MCP -> TS : PUT /api/v2026.2/projects/{p}/findings/flagged
    TS --> MCP : ok
    MCP --> Agent : ok
end

Agent --> Dev : summary — fixed / tolerated / skipped

@enduml
